d  to me when I was on travel with this  person if there had been clear rules  guidelines the do's and don'ts when  you're away from the office maybe those  things wouldn't have happened in the  first instance so I think that the onus  really is on the employer to set those  guidelines to make sure that they're not  having company events that are going  late into the night where there is  alcohol being served as an example these  kinds of things I mean you take a few of  these steps to ensure that you know your  people are are in continue to be in safe  spaces then the chances that that you're  going to have people who will slip is is  much reduced we've been speaking with  attorney Scott Oswald he is an attorney  who represents employees he's also  managing principal of the Employment Law  Group a very important and timely topic  Scott thanks so much for talking to us  about it hey David you're welcome it is  my pleasure

